{
  "id": "Compound::DB00898 - Gene::2741",
  "verbalization": "Ethanol is implicated in the interaction with Glra1 through a series of molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that ethanol binds to Glra2, a receptor subunit, which then participates in various ion channel activities, including extracellular-glycine-gated, extracellular-chloride-gated, and inhibitory extracellular ligand-gated ion channel activities. These activities are all associated with Glra1, indicating a potential functional link between ethanol and Glra1. The overlapping roles of Glra2 in different ion channel activities suggest that ethanol may influence Glra1 through a mechanism involving receptor modulation or functional activation of Glra1. The consistent binding of ethanol to Glra2 and its association with Glra1 highlights a possible role in modulating ion channel function, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
